WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.200
-Welcome to the show.
And also welcome to NBC.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.234
-Thank you.
I'm so thrilled to be here.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.567
You have no idea.

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:09.567
-You have been called the
Godfather of Fantasy Football,

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.767
and you've done
a lot of cool things.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:13.534
I think one of
the coolest things is that

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:18.567
you helped a lot of the Avengers
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:20.100
play fantasy football.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.767
And, in fact, they liked you
so much that you're in --

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:24.200
-I was texting with
Chris Pratt today.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.534
He wants to know Elijah Mitchell
or Rashaad Penny Week 1.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:27.801
Elijah Mitchell is the answer.

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:28.901
-Wow.
-I'm just saying.

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:30.100
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.667
-Well, here you are in
a pretty massive scene of

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:34.434
"Avengers: Endgame."

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:37.501
This is Robert Redford, you,
Robert Downey Jr.,

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:38.801
and Chris Hemsworth.

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:41.200
And did you --
I'm not being rude.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.467
Did you have
a speaking line in the --

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:45.100
-I had four lines,
believe it or not.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.467
Like, no,
when you watch it, Jimmy,

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:47.934
when you watch it back,
because I know that's what

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:50.434
you're going to do tonight,
just put on the closed caption.

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:51.901
I'm only on camera
for one of them.

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:52.968
Three big stars.

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:54.667
But I got four lines.
I'm in the cast.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:55.868
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:58.601
-So IMDb, you're in the cast?
-I'm in the cast.

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.534
I'm part of the MCU. I'm canon.

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:03.501
I have my own page
on the Marvel Wiki.

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.734
Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:08.601
-Wow.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:09.767
-That's fantastic.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.634
Is that your only film
you've been in?

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.067
-Yes, it is.

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.067
And, by the way,
so, "Avengers: Endgame,"

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.901
as you guys know,
is the highest-grossing movie

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.901
of all time worldwide, okay?

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.834
And it's the only movie
I have been in.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:24.667
So, I mean, people want to talk
about Tom Cruise or The Rock

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.868
and their total box office,
but I'm just saying,

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:29.767
if you look at the stats,
which is what I do,

00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:33.434
on a per-movie basis,
I'm the highest-grossing actor

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:34.734
of all time worldwide.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:37.767
-Oh, my gosh. It's amazing.
-Numbers are numbers.

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.634
-Numbers are numbers.
-I'm just saying.

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:42.434
I've retired from movies.
I'm never going to do it.

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:44.467
So until some movie beats
"Avengers: Endgame,"

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:45.801
like, I'm the guy.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:49.767
-Yeah. I wanted to talk to you
about fantasy football

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:53.300
and when it got popular
and did you ever see yourself

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:57.467
as being the top analyst or
even having a career

00:01:57.467 --> 00:01:59.567
based on fantasy football
when you were a kid?

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.334
-No. You know, I do
these interviews sometimes,

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:02.501
and people say like,
"Oh, is this your dream job?"

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:03.734
I'm like, "No."

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:05.934
When I was dreaming of jobs,
this didn't exist.

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:07.133
You know what I mean?

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:10.067
Like, fantasy football
was like a sports version

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:11.400
of "Dungeons &amp; Dragons."

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.434
Like, it was this
nerdy, niche thing.

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:16.467
And so the idea that I could
somehow make a living

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.334
wearing makeup, being on TV,

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:22.133
talking about fake football
was, you know, asinine to me.

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:25.300
And, you know, so, the fact that
I was in "Avengers: Endgame,"

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.300
the fact that I'm
on "The Tonight Show" --

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.100
I'm on the "The Tonight Show
with Jimmy Fallon."

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.400
What's better than that?
-Yeah.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.534
-I mean, right?
-No, I'm happy.

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:35.300
-This is cool.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.567
-I'm happy --
Now, also, you're involved --

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:39.634
You're part of
"Football Night in America."

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:41.601
You're on the team
now here at NBC.

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:43.834
So now, yeah,
we share the same locker room.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:44.934
-Yeah.

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:47.767
-Yeah, so, but
after the show, weirdly,

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.701
tonight,
"The Tonight Show" staff --

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:50.834
we're all getting together.

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:53.334
We're doing
the fantasy-football draft.

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:55.601
I have no idea what I'm doing.

00:02:55.601 --> 00:02:57.667
-Okay. I can help.
This is what I do.

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:59.133
-Yeah.
-We're colleagues now.

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:00.901
-Yeah.
-You can e-mail me.

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:02.801
-I can?
-I'll get my number to you.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:03.834
You'll text me. Yeah.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:05.334
Wait. 'Cause, listen, it's

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:07.367
"The Tonight Show
with Jimmy Fallon" League.

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:09.200
Jimmy Fallon can't finish last.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.200
We can't have you
doing some sort of punishment

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.467
or anything like that.

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:13.968
Like, I feel like we need to get
you to the playoffs,

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:15.033
but not win.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.667
Like, so you look good,

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.801
but you don't crush
staff morale.

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:20.033
-Oh, yeah, I understand.
-You're the star.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.434
-Yeah, yeah, you're very smart.
-You're the star.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.534
-Yeah, you don't want me
to win...

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:23.834
-Right, right.

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.467
-...but just get far enough
to show that I could win.

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:26.601
-Exactly. You could win,

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:27.868
and you're just
sort of taking it easy.

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:29.734
-Just for anyone watching,
the first one,

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:32.501
everyone's like,
"Oh, you got to get..."

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:35.367
-Right. Well, so, I know --

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:36.667
I talked to
your producer backstage.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:38.033
You have the second pick.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.968
You have pick 2 this year.
-I have pick 2. That's big deal.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.234
-Right. So, most likely,
Jonathan Taylor will go 1.

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:44.367
He's the Colts' running back,
had a great season last year.

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.501
So, my question to you is,
what kind of player are you?

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:48.467
Like, do you want to be
risk-averse

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:50.133
or are you gonna
swing for the fences?

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:52.701
Because I'm a believer in,
you know,

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:54.200
Ricky Bobby from
"Talladega Nights."

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.000
Like, if you ain't first,
you're last, right?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.968
If I were you, at pick 2,
I'm taking Christian McCaffrey,

00:03:57.968 --> 00:03:59.734
who's been hurt
the last two years,

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:00.934
but, when he is healthy,

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:02.701
has been the best player
in fantasy football.

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:05.234
So, again,
it's a risk/reward pick.

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:06.234
That's what I would do at 2.

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:07.601
That's who I have
ranked number 2.

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:10.267
-Now, when you
say things like this,

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:13.801
does it throw the numbers,
like, crazy?

00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:14.834
Maybe.
-Somewhat.

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:15.834
Yeah, I mean, I don't know.

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:17.200
You know, yes.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.801
I mean, I'm flattered that a lot
of people pay attention to

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:19.901
what I say.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.067
-So you can make up a name.

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:23.934
You're like, "Oh,
you got to get Skip Benson."

00:04:23.934 --> 00:04:25.634
-Right. Yeah.
-And you go, "Who's that?"

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:28.267
-Dougle McGillicuddy at
running back is a sleeper.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:32.067
Yeah, but most -- In the
fantasy-football industry,

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:34.801
most people have McCaffrey
at number 2 or 1.

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:37.667
Yeah. So that's not
a controversial take by me.

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.767
-So, you will help me out?
-I will help you out.

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:42.634
I've got your back.
By the way, do you want to win?

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:45.467
I mean, like, you can --
Because, like, yeah,

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.667
I mean, if you want to,
I will help you

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.501
crush your staff like a grape.

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:51.601
You know, let's do it.
-Yes! Yes!

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:55.200
-Like, I was trying to be nice.
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.801
I'm taking out Kamal.
I'm taking Kamal out.

00:04:57.801 --> 00:04:59.934
I'm taking Kamal out.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:01.567
Matthew Berry,
I appreciate you, buddy.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:02.701
-Hey, thanks for having me,
Jimmy.

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.200
-Thanks for being here.
-My pleasure.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.534
-Matthew Berry.

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:08.300
Watch "Fantasy Football
Happy Hour" weekdays on Peacock.

